    46	**Motion findings:** motion instants — icon exit + tile entry ≈1200–5500 ms (Pennsylvania first, small→full; Virginia staggered behind it) · free lines land ≈5000–6000 ms · frame + enslaved lines ≈8500–10000 ms · clause tag lands ≈12500–14000 ms · squares + numerals land ≈15000–17500 ms (staggered fade grey→black). Holds — icon 0–~1200 ms · free-count board ≈6000–8500 ms · framed board ≈10000–12500 ms · tagged board ≈14000–15000 ms · completed scoreboard ≈17500–20500 ms. No dissolves between beats; each element lands and persists (accumulation grammar).
    47	**Sub-beats:** SB-A clause icon + banner hold, icon exits · SB-B tiles scale in (PA first, VA staggered) · SB-C free-people lines land · SB-D Virginia frame draws on + enslaved-people lines land · SB-E clause tag lands on the frame · SB-F square grids + verdict numerals land on both flanks · SB-G completed scoreboard hold. (Portrait coda SB-H is DEFERRED — §2.3.)
    48	
    49	### 1.4 Variables (§1.3 extraction)
    50	1. State set + order (2 states in the specimen) — per state: label, enslaved count, free count, elector count, tagged flag (which tile carries the clause frame + tag).
    51	2. Icon — presence, fraction split (3/5), icon colours, banner text, banner colours.
    52	3. Tile geometry — tile size, positions/gap, silhouette presence (generic silhouette path per state is data, drawn from CONFIG points — NOT a traced frame: silhouettes are simplified polygons named in CONFIG).
    53	4. Frame — tagged tile's frame width/colour, draw duration.
    54	5. Tag — text, tilt angle, colours, position on the frame corner.
    55	6. Population lines — row labels ("Enslaved people:" / "Free people:"), number formatting (comma-grouped), label/number font sizes, row colours (enslaved numerals in frame orange, free numerals in ink).
    56	7. Squares — per-state elector count, grid columns, square size/pitch, fill colour, per-square stagger + fade duration, numeral text/size (numeral = the count itself, derived), and FILL ORDER (jev-observe-exit charge, applied): traversal is row-major (left→right, top→bottom) within each grid, both grids starting together at tSquaresMs — carried as CONFIG key `fillOrder: "row-major"` with its derivation in §2.1 (the T208 fillOrder cure, carried forward).
    57	8. Timing — icon hold/exit, tile start/duration/stagger, free start/duration, frame start/duration, tag start/duration, squares start/stagger/fade, final hold, total duration.
    58	9. Palette — paper ground, tile slate, tile-name pale, frame/tag orange, banner red/teal, icon orange/dark, square black, ink, muted label grey.
    59	10. Easing — per-phase easing names.
    60	
    61	### 1.5 Guidance dispositions (inline, A9.5)
    62	- A1 §2 typography precedent (runtime sampling of config-rendered text): NOT APPLICABLE — no particle typography; all text is SVG text rendered from CONFIG strings/numbers, the same config-driven principle in its DOM/SVG form. Reason stated here per A9.5.
    63	- A5 Owner Cures 1–2 (intensity separation · phrase exclusivity): NOT APPLICABLE as particle/sequence cures — no particle field, no phrase lifecycle. The analogous separation here is construction-level: the tagged tile is separated by a *frame + tag* (a different kind of mark), never by intensity alone — priced in Plan. Phase exclusivity DOES apply in its sequencing form: each sub-beat's landing completes before the next begins (phase-order invariant, §2.1).
    64	- A5 §4 flow-field model: NOT APPLICABLE — no particle pool exists in this technique.
    65	- Family: Packet #12 counting siblings (T208 paired dot counts · T210 threshold grid map · T212 margin bar field) — count-board geometry from CONFIG arrays is the family's demonstrated construction; T212's filed lesson (receipt-form discipline, A12/A13) is carried into §2.4 planning.
    66	
    67	## §2 — PLAN
    68	
    69	### 2.1 Parameter table (every variable → CONFIG key; specimen value = default)
    70	Top-level: `stageW 640 · stageH 440 · tileW 118 · tileH 118 · tileY 92 · tileGapPx 150 (centre-to-centre offset from stage centre ±) · frameWidthPx 13 · tagAngleDeg -4 · tagFontPx 11 · nameFontPx 19 · rowLabelFontPx 15 · rowNumFontPx 27 · numeralFontPx 30 · squareSizePx 13 · squarePitchPx 19 · gridCols 5 · fillOrder "row-major" · iconFraction 0.6 · tIconMs 0 · iconHoldMs 1200 · iconOutDurMs 600 · tTilesMs 1800 · tileDurMs 2200 · tileStaggerMs 500 · tFreeMs 5000 · freeDurMs 600 · tFrameMs 8500 · frameDurMs 1000 · tTagMs 12500 · tagDurMs 500 · tSquaresMs 15000 · squareFadeMs 400 · squareStaggerMs 55 · holdMs 9500 · easeIcon/easeTile/easeFade/easeFrame/easeSquares all "easeInOut" · palette {ground #f4f1ea, tile #46585c, tileName #dfe9e6, silhouette #3a4c50, frame #c96f4a, tagBg #c4453c, tagAlt #2f6f79, bannerBg #c4453c, bannerAlt #2f6f79, iconTop #d2691e, iconBottom #33484d, square #141414, ink #2b2b2b, muted #6d6d6d, enslavedNum #c96f4a} · fontFamily "Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif" · clauseText "Three-fifths clause" · enslavedLabel "Enslaved people:" · freeLabel "Free people:"`.
    71	Nested: `states[2]` — `{label, enslaved, free, electors, tagged, silhouette}`: Virginia {347000, 539000, 21, true, simplified polygon points} · Pennsylvania {1700, 601000, 15, false, simplified polygon points}. Silhouette polygons are coarse CONFIG point lists (a generic state-ish outline per tile), priced as decoration-level geometry — the technique is the count board, not cartography.
    72	Derived (named, not stored): tile x positions (stage centre ∓ tileGapPx, order = states order BUT entry order is entryOrder per state — see below) · entry order: Pennsylvania enters first, Virginia second — carried as `states[].enterIdx` (PA 0, VA 1) so the stagger binds to data, not position · square positions (gridCols columns, rows = ceil(electors/gridCols), flanking outward from each tile) · numeral text = String(electors) · formatted counts = comma-grouping of the CONFIG numbers · **phase-order invariant (validation-enforced):** tTiles ≥ icon exit end · tFree ≥ last tile end · tFrame ≥ free end · tTag ≥ frame end · tSquares ≥ tag end — a CONFIG violating the order is rejected by validateConfig, never rendered overlapped. **Count assertion (A9.3):** source counts — states 2, electors 21 + 15 = 36 — vs built counts printed by the harness; mismatch halts.
    73	Complete-at: squares last = tSquaresMs + (maxElectors−1)·squareStaggerMs + squareFadeMs = 15000 + 20·55 + 400 = 16500… — NOTE: census CP8 (16000 ms) shows squares mid-landing and CP9 (18000) complete; 16500 complete is inside that bracket ✓. durationMs = completeAt + holdMs = 16500 + 9500 = 26000 (window length; holdMs set 9500 so the board holds to the window end under the departure in §2.3).
    74	
    75	### 2.2 Construction choice
    76	**DOM/SVG tiles + square grids (chosen):** one SVG scene; a person-icon group (circle + body path split at the CONFIG fraction into two fills), banner rect + text, per-state tile group (rect + silhouette polygon + name), frame rect (tagged state only), tag group (rotated rect + text), two population text rows per state, per-state square grid of rects + numeral text — all geometry/opacity from `stateAt(cfg,t)`, a pure function evaluable in node.
    77	Rejected: Canvas 2D — loses per-element ink measurement the A6 fit leg needs. CSS keyframes — phase state not evaluable as a pure function (A11 receipts impossible). HTML divs — SVG gives exact geometry for harness receipts at less code.
    78	
    79	### 2.3 Census-anchor mapping (A10.2) + A11 assertions
    80	Window-start offset: segment-anchored, build 0 ms = source 305000 ms. **Departure table:** ONE departure — SB-H portrait coda (census CP11–CP12, 22000–24000 ms): a photographic painting slides up and covers the board. DEFERRED with reason: photographic content cannot be recreated by code/generated construction without specimen media or tracing (§6.1 refusal class), and it is not the count-board technique — it is the narration's payoff image. The build instead HOLDS the completed scoreboard from completeAt (16500 ms) to durationMs (26000 ms); CP13 (26000 ms) is the next technique (T220) and asserts nothing about T219. All other checkpoints map 1:1.
    81	Assertions (each: CONFIG expression → evaluated instant):
    82	- CP0 zero/icon: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tIconMs)` → 0 ms: iconP=1, banner present, tiles scale 0, squares 0. (Zero-state anchor for tiles/squares, guards cmd 8.)
    83	- P1 icon exit: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.iconHoldMs + CONFIG.iconOutDurMs)` → 1800 ms: iconP=0.
    84	- C@2000: `stateAt(CONFIG, 2000)`: PA (enterIdx 0) tileP = easeTile(clamp01((2000−tTilesMs)/tileDurMs)) > 0; VA (enterIdx 1) tileP = 0 (its staggered start = tTilesMs + tileStaggerMs = 2300 > 2000). Order receipt.
    85	- P2 tiles complete: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tTilesMs + CONFIG.tileStaggerMs + CONFIG.tileDurMs)` → 4500 ms: both tileP=1, freeP=0.
