**REVISE — T219, Cycle 039 Wave 36 §2 gate-out.** The SVG count-board construction is sound. The plan still has unbound controls and a payoff checkpoint that a mistimed build could pass.

1. **Convergent freeze — CLEAR by construction.** T15’s motion and reusability lenses scored 68 and 64 and both identified the frozen surplus during formation. T219’s `stateAt(cfg,t)` evaluates each square’s reveal from time and index. There is no shared pool, borrowing, or velocity state, so the T15 defect has no equivalent path. The completed scoreboard hold is intentional. [T15 scores, attempt 1](/home/hatch/workspace/goals/diy-building-and-real-learning/hidden_files/study/recreations/T15-particle-typography/scores.md:25) · [T219 Plan §§2.1–2.3](runs/2026-11-18-cycle-039-wave-36/item-T219-observe-plan.md:69)

2. **Owner catches — CLEAR on visual separation, REVISE on sequencing coverage.** The `tagged` flag controls whether the frame and tag exist, giving the tile a distinct mark even when colors change. Phrase exclusivity is inapplicable. The analogous rule for landing phases is enforceable if validation and rendering share the same phase boundaries. P1 currently omits `tIconMs` from the icon exit expression, so the zero default hides a failure if the icon start moves. Derive icon exit as `tIconMs + iconHoldMs + iconOutDurMs` and last tile end from the maximum validated `enterIdx`. Use those same boundaries in rendering, validation, and probes. Include a nonzero icon-start test that rejects a tile start before the icon exits. [T219 Plan §§2.1–2.4](runs/2026-11-18-cycle-039-wave-36/item-T219-observe-plan.md:69)

3. **Parameterization — REVISE.** Observe names icon presence, silhouette presence, and tag position. Plan leaves icon presence and tag placement without a CONFIG binding or derivation, and leaves silhouette omission undefined. Bind icon presence, define a nullable silhouette, and derive the tag anchor from frame geometry and named offsets. Specify how `fillOrder` maps reveal indices to coordinates on both flanks. A mirrored grid can have the right count and still reverse the recorded left-to-right reveal. The swap fixture retains the `true, false` tag pattern, so it can pass with a hardcoded first-slot tag. Flip the tagged slot and supply complete state fixtures, including `enterIdx`. Finally, resolve the color contract. If `palette.frame` controls both frame and enslaved numerals, derive both from it and remove the duplicate `enslavedNum` key. Otherwise test the two controls independently. [T219 Observe §1.4 and Plan §§2.1–2.4](runs/2026-11-18-cycle-039-wave-36/item-T219-observe-plan.md:49) · [T208 scores, completion cure for `fillOrder`](/home/hatch/workspace/goals/diy-building-and-real-learning/hidden_files/study/recreations/T208-paired-dot-counts-house-stage/scores.md:60)

4. **Bar arithmetic — credible minimum, weak motion proof.** Motion fidelity is a defensible predicted minimum. T210’s filed lenses sum to `72 + 90 + 98 + 78 + 88 = 426`, or **85.2**, with motion lowest at **72**. That is one point above the required total of **425**. A motion score of 72 leaves the other four lenses needing **353**, or **88.25** on average. T208 and T212 have no filed five-lens scores in the records reviewed. T219’s default timing arithmetic is correct at **16,500 ms complete** and **26,000 ms total**, but P4 can pass with a uniform fade because it checks only aggregate visibility and positive numeral opacity. Price that risk before the portrait deferral. At 16,000 ms, the planned stagger puts Virginia’s first square fully on, square index 14 in flight, and square index 20 still off. Assert those states and the numeral’s presence, then move the probe with the square timing swap. CP1 likewise needs the recorded approximate Pennsylvania scale as a target. `tileP > 0` proves entry order alone. [T210 scores, lens table](/home/hatch/workspace/goals/diy-building-and-real-learning/hidden_files/study/recreations/T210-threshold-grid-map/scores.md:43) · [T219 census and Plan §§2.1–2.5](runs/2026-11-18-cycle-039-wave-36/item-T219-observe-plan.md:29)

5. **Size discipline — CLEAR.** The population rows, clause marker, and square-grid payoff form one count-board mechanic. The plan defers the photographic portrait, caps silhouettes at simple polygons, and treats the next technique as outside T219. [T219 Plan §§2.1–2.3](runs/2026-11-18-cycle-039-wave-36/item-T219-observe-plan.md:69) · [Recreation instruction §8](INSTRUCTION.md:65)

**Limits.** This is a pre-Execute review. T219’s build record, rendered fit, and motion were not assessed. Census comparisons use the observations filed in the item record.

